tools/pre-push.sh runs CI's quick checks before a push, in a few seconds: check_versions.py, check_manifest.py
against what the remote has (the check the release push of 15-10-2026 failed on: apps.toml changed without the portal
bump), the exec bits and the line endings of the pushed commit. tools/hooks/pre-push makes it git's pre-push hook
(git config core.hooksPath tools/hooks); BC250_PRE_PUSH=full also runs tools/ci-local.sh, git push --no-verify skips
it. Tests in tools/tests/test_pre_push.py. fix-modes.sh and CI's exec-bit check cover tools/hooks/ too, CI
shellchecks the hook, and the development page of the wiki and CLAUDE.md name it.

