Changelog: 09-10-2026 22:59:08

Docs: the manual (MkDocs Material) holds everything the READMEs held: one chapter per app, the portal, a Development
chapter (the root README's layout, development, install locations and versions sections, core's README and Bazzite
Test's development notes) and Security (docs/SECURITY.md, which GitHub also shows as the security policy). It has the
apps' look: Bazzite purple (#5835CE, #8A2BE2), Inter, a light and a dark mode, and the suite icon.
tools/mkdocs/hooks.py serves the app icons and screenshots from where they live. The root README is a short
description with one line and the small icon per app.

.github/workflows/docs.yml publishes the manual on GitHub Pages from main. tools/stage_app.py adds an app's chapter to
its release as MANUAL.md.

